  "story": "The weekend's results confirmed what many had been sensing for months - the tectonic plates of Super League were shifting from one side of the Pennines to the other. From a particular angle, watching Hull KR dismantle their opponents revealed a team that was no longer just a contender but a genuine force to be reckoned with. The image of the Robins moving within just three wins of their first major trophy in almost 40 years would dominate every magazine cover come the final days of the season. The club had become a rock on which to build a dynasty, just as Wigan and St Helens had been for the previous half-decade. Every weekend, the question would be asked: when will they falter? But each answer was emphatic, as the Robins delivered yet another destructive display. At Old Trafford in mid-October, the biggest prize awaited. For a side without a piece of silverware since 1985, the prospect of finishing top and claiming the League Leader's Shield was a dream no longer out of reach. The Huddersfield, Castleford, and Warrington cautionary tales echoed in the mind of every fan, a reminder that being table-toppers does not guarantee glory. Yet here was Hull KR, proving they were different - and the coming weeks would reveal if the tectonic shift was truly complete."
